    sections:[['The decision boundary','The three models solve different kinds of uncertainty.',[['Choose advisory','Use it when leadership needs to prioritise opportunities, test feasibility, or set an investment and governance boundary.'],['Choose custom development','Use it when users, workflow, integrations, and acceptance criteria can be defined before implementation.'],['Choose FDE','Use it when the valuable problem is known but the correct intervention must be learned from real operations.']]],['Signals you chose the wrong model','A mismatch appears early if the engagement is measured against the wrong unit of success.',[['Advice without a decision','A strategy project is incomplete if nobody owns the resulting choice and next gate.'],['Build without a stable boundary','A fixed specification fails when core requirements change as operators see working software.'],['FDE without field access','Embedded delivery cannot work without operator participation, evidence access, and an accountable outcome owner.']]]],
    steps:[['Name the decision','State what must be decided or changed and who owns it.'],['Score uncertainty','Separate uncertainty about value, workflow, data, integration, and adoption.'],['Choose the smallest complete model','Buy only enough engagement to resolve the material uncertainty.'],['Set an exit gate','Define evidence for scaling, changing course, or stopping.']],
